################ p5_neighbours.sh
=== Elixir 1.14: elixirc on a call to an absent module
warning: Req.new/1 is undefined (module Req is not available or is yet to be defined)
  a.ex:2: A.f/0

(elixirc exit=0)

=== Elixir 1.14: mix, a module of an app the project does not depend on (Logger without :logger in extra_applications)
warning: Logger.__do_log__/4 defined in application :logger is used by the current application but the current application does not depend on :logger. To fix this, you must do one of:

  1. If :logger is part of Erlang/Elixir, you must include it under :extra_applications inside "def application" in your mix.exs

  2. If :logger is a dependency, make sure it is listed under "def deps" in your mix.exs

  3. In case you don't want to add a requirement to :logger, you may optionally skip this warning by adding [xref: [exclude: [Logger]]] to your "def project" in mix.exs


=== Erlang: erlc, absent module (no check) then xref (the check lives in a separate tool)
(erlc exit=0 -> compiled without complaint)
xref undefined_function_calls = {ok,[{{b,f,0},{nosuch,call,1}}]}

=== Erlang release: .app `applications` is enforced by systools, not by the compiler
    [{error_reading,{fakereq,{not_found,"fakereq.app"}}},

